  "answer": "",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "Substitute b = ak into 3b³ − b² + 5b.",
    "Every term now has a factor of a. Factor it out; what's left is the witness."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Since $a \\mid b$, $b = ak$ for some integer $k$.",
    "$3b^3 - b^2 + 5b = 3a^3k^3 - a^2k^2 + 5ak = a(3a^2k^3 - ak^2 + 5k)$.",
    "$3a^2k^3 - ak^2 + 5k$ is an integer, so $a \\mid (3b^3 - b^2 + 5b)$. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "hammack-bop3",
    "section": "Chapter 4 exercises, #10 (p. 126)",
    "note": "This exact exercise, restated in ProofLab's words. Uses Definition 4.4 (divides)."
  },
